---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Dryland Runner: 7,000 years in a drying Sahara" description="A one-button game: 10,500 years ago the Sahara was green. Choose how your people live as it slowly turns to desert, and see if they make it.">
  <div class="wrap page dr-page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="crumb"><a href="/lab">Lab</a></p>
      <h1>Dryland Runner</h1>
      <p>Ten thousand years ago the Sahara was green. Then, slowly, it turned to desert. Choose how your people live, and see if they make it.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="game" aria-label="The game">
      <div class="hud" aria-live="off">
        <div class="when">
          <span id="h-ago" class="ago">10,525 years ago</span>
          <span class="sub"><span id="h-year">8500 BCE</span>, <span id="h-era">the Green Sahara</span></span>
        </div>
        <div class="meters">
          <div class="meter m-water"><span class="lab">Water</span><div class="bar"><i id="b-water"></i></div><span id="n-water" class="num">80</span></div>
          <div class="meter m-food"><span class="lab">Food</span><div class="bar"><i id="b-food"></i></div><span id="n-food" class="num">80</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="stage" id="stage">
        <canvas id="cv" width="960" height="400" aria-label="Your person walking through a changing landscape" role="img"></canvas>
        <p id="banner" class="banner" hidden></p>
        <button id="pause" class="pause" type="button" hidden>Pause</button>

        <div id="ov-start" class="ov">
          <div class="ov-box key-box">
            <h2>The Sahara, 10,500 years ago</h2>
            <p>It is green, with lakes and grassland. Over the next 7,000 years it will slowly dry into desert. Keep your people alive.</p>
            <div class="key">
              <div class="key-group">
                <h3>Walk into these</h3>
                <ul>
                  <li><canvas data-icon="water"></canvas><span><strong class="t-water">Water</strong>: a waterhole where your people drink</span></li>
                  <li><canvas data-icon="well"></canvas><span><strong class="t-water">Water</strong>: a well, once you dig them</span></li>
                  <li><canvas data-icon="fish"></canvas><span><strong class="t-food">Food</strong>: fish</span></li>
                  <li><canvas data-icon="grain"></canvas><span><strong class="t-food">Food</strong>: wild grain</span></li>
                  <li><canvas data-icon="field"></canvas><span><strong class="t-food">Food</strong>: your fields, once you farm</span></li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="key-group">
                <h3>Jump to catch</h3>
                <ul>
                  <li><canvas data-icon="game"></canvas><span><strong class="t-food">Food</strong>: gazelle</span></li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Jump over</h3>
                <ul>
                  <li class="row3"><canvas data-icon="rock"></canvas><canvas data-icon="thorn"></canvas><canvas data-icon="dune"></canvas><span>Rocks, thorns and dunes cost water and food</span></li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="keys"><span class="touch-only">Tap the game to jump.</span><span class="no-touch">Press space, or click the game, to jump.</span> A few times along the way, you’ll choose how your people live.</p>
            <button id="go" class="btn" type="button">Start</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="ov-gate" class="ov" hidden>
          <div class="ov-box wide">
            <h2>What should your people do?</h2>
            <p id="g-sit" class="sit"></p>
            <div id="g-opts" class="opts"></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="ov-paused" class="ov" hidden>
          <div class="ov-box"><h2>Paused</h2><button id="resume" class="btn" type="button">Carry on</button></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="turn">On a phone, turn it sideways for a bigger view.</p>
      <ul id="ways" class="ways" aria-label="Your choices and how they are doing"></ul>
    </section>

    <section id="end" class="end" hidden aria-live="polite">
      <h2 id="e-title"></h2>
      <div id="e-text" class="e-text"></div>
      <figure class="chart">
        <svg id="e-chart" viewBox="0 0 760 280" role="img" aria-label="Your water and food over time, with rainfall and your choices"></svg>
        <figcaption><span class="k k-rain"></span>Rain <span class="k k-water"></span>Your water <span class="k k-food"></span>Your food <span class="k k-spell"></span>Dry spells</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="real">
        <h3>Your choices: what they gave you, and what really happened</h3>
        <ul id="e-real" class="e-real"></ul>
        <h3>The bigger picture</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>The Sahara was green because of a slow wobble in Earth’s orbit that made the African monsoon stronger. As it weakened, the rains moved south.</li>
          <li>The eastern Sahara was home to people from about 8500 BCE. After about 5300 BCE it dried, and by 3500 BCE most had left for the Nile valley, the oases and the south.</li>
          <li>In Africa, herding came before farming. Sorghum and millet were only domesticated after 3500 BCE, when the desert was already spreading.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <button id="again" class="btn" type="button">Play again</button>
    </section>

    <section class="notes">
      <div>
        <h2>Behind the game</h2>
        <p>The climate follows a reconstruction of the eastern Sahara by Kuper and Kröpelin (2006). Every choice is something people really did, and the facts behind your choices appear when the game ends.</p>
        <p>The numbers are made up so that choices matter. One second is 40 years, and dry spells come at random.</p>
        <p>The hindsight at the end comes from replaying the rest of history four times with each option you could have picked, played by a steady computer player.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>After you play</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Did a choice that worked early let you down later? Why?</li>
          <li>In Africa, herding came before farming. Why might animals, which you can move, suit a climate you can’t predict?</li>
          <li>Sharing costs a little every day but saves you in a crisis. Where do people make that trade today?</li>
          <li>Which of these ways of living still exist in the Sahel today?</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sources">
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Kuper, R. &amp; Kröpelin, S. (2006). Climate-controlled Holocene occupation in the Sahara: motor of Africa’s evolution. <em>Science</em> 313, 803–807. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1130989">doi:10.1126/science.1130989</a></li>
        <li>Huysecom, E. et al. (2009). The emergence of pottery in Africa during the tenth millennium cal BC: new evidence from Ounjougou (Mali). <em>Antiquity</em> 83, 905–917. <a href="https://doi.org/10.1017/S0003598X00099245">doi:10.1017/S0003598X00099245</a></li>
        <li>Sutton, J. E. G. (1977). The African aqualithic. <em>Antiquity</em> 51, 25–34.</li>
        <li>Marshall, F. &amp; Hildebrand, E. (2002). Cattle before crops: the beginnings of food production in Africa. <em>Journal of World Prehistory</em> 16, 99–143.</li>
        <li>Winchell, F. et al. (2017). Evidence for sorghum domestication in fourth-millennium BC eastern Sudan. <em>Current Anthropology</em> 58, 673–683.</li>
        <li>Manning, K. et al. (2011). 4500-year old domesticated pearl millet from the Tilemsi Valley, Mali. <em>Journal of Archaeological Science</em> 38, 312–322.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="made">Made for outreach in the <a href="https://agri-dry.org">AGRI-DRY</a> doctoral network, which studies farming in drylands past and present. Spotted something wrong? <a href="/#contact">Tell me</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<script>
  import * as M from '../../lib/dryland-model';

  const $ = <T extends HTMLElement = HTMLElement>(id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as T;
  const cv = $<HTMLCanvasElement>('cv');
  let ctx = cv.getContext('2d')!;
  const W = 960, H = 400;
  let VW = 960; // visible width of the world; narrower on phones so things stay big
  const reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
  const NOW = new Date().getFullYear();
  const touch = window.matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches;
  document.documentElement.classList.toggle('is-touch', touch);

  let s = M.newState();
  let mode: 'start' | 'run' | 'gate' | 'pause' | 'end' = 'start';
  let last = 0;
  let scroll = 0; // total px travelled, for the scenery

  // ---------- colour ----------
  type Pal = Record<string, [string, string]>; // [wet, dry]
  const DAY: Pal = {
    sky: ['#cfe4e6', '#eee2c9'], skyLow: ['#e6f0ea', '#f5ead2'], far: ['#9dbca3', '#dcc08f'], mid: ['#6f9a63', '#c9a66b'],
    ground: ['#7c9a52', '#d2a564'], path: ['#9b7b52', '#b8875a'], tree: ['#3f6b3a', '#7c6a3e'], trunk: ['#5c4630', '#5c4630'],
    lake: ['#5b9cbf', '#8fb6c4'], tuft: ['#56803f', '#a88a4c'], sun: ['#f2c25b', '#f0a842'],
  };
  const NIGHT: Pal = {
    sky: ['#14232a', '#2a2418'], skyLow: ['#1d3330', '#3a3020'], far: ['#25402f', '#4d3f28'], mid: ['#2f5034', '#63502f'],
    ground: ['#334f2d', '#6e5633'], path: ['#4a3a26', '#5a4529'], tree: ['#5d9a5a', '#8d7a48'], trunk: ['#7a6248', '#7a6248'],
    lake: ['#3f7396', '#55707a'], tuft: ['#6c9e55', '#9a8046'], sun: ['#e8e4cf', '#e8d9b0'],
  };
  const INK = { day: { ink: '#11252b', water: '#1f6fa3', food: '#a85a06', hurt: '#8a2b1a', mud: '#7a6142', shine: '#cfe6f2', trunk: '#5c4630', rock: '#62574c', thorn: '#3c3a28', dune: '#c99a55', duneEdge: '#a77a3c', cow: '#f2ede2', cowSpot: '#5a4434', fish: '#2e5f73', grain: '#b0741b', stalk: '#6e7f3b', game: '#8a5a32', pot: '#b36a2b' },
               night: { ink: '#e6ece4', water: '#7cc0ea', food: '#e8b25c', hurt: '#f08a6a', mud: '#4a3a26', shine: '#e2f2fb', trunk: '#8a7050', rock: '#8c8070', thorn: '#a7a07a', dune: '#a98049', duneEdge: '#7d5d33', cow: '#e9e3d4', cowSpot: '#4a382a', fish: '#8cc4d4', grain: '#e0a648', stalk: '#9fb06a', game: '#c39260', pot: '#d48a4b' } };
  const night = () => document.documentElement.dataset.theme === 'night';
  const hex = (h: string) => [1, 3, 5].map((i) => parseInt(h.slice(i, i + 2), 16));
  const mix = (a: string, b: string, t: number) => { const A = hex(a), B = hex(b); return `rgb(${A.map((v, i) => Math.round(v + (B[i] - v) * t)).join(',')})`; };
  const col = (k: string, dry: number) => { const p = (night() ? NIGHT : DAY)[k]; return mix(p[0], p[1], Math.max(0, Math.min(1, dry))); };
  const ink = () => (night() ? INK.night : INK.day);

  // ---------- canvas sizing ----------
  function fit() {
    const dpr = Math.min(2, window.devicePixelRatio || 1);
    VW = ($('stage').clientWidth || 960) < 640 ? 600 : 960;
    cv.style.aspectRatio = `${VW} / ${H}`;
    const w = cv.clientWidth;
    cv.width = Math.round(w * dpr); cv.height = Math.round((w * H / VW) * dpr);
    ctx.setTransform(cv.width / VW, 0, 0, cv.height / H, 0, 0);
  }
  window.addEventListener('resize', () => { fit(); draw(); });

  // ---------- scenery ----------
  const hash = (n: number) => { const x = Math.sin(n * 127.1) * 43758.5453; return x - Math.floor(x); };

  function draw() {
    const r = M.localRain(s);
    const dry = 1 - Math.min(1, r / 0.9);
    const lake = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (r - 0.45) / 0.4));
    const K = ink();
    const off = reduce ? 0 : scroll;

    // sky
    const g = ctx.createLinearGradient(0, 0, 0, 260);
    g.addColorStop(0, col('sky', dry)); g.addColorStop(1, col('skyLow', dry));
    ctx.fillStyle = g; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
    ctx.fillStyle = col('sun', dry);
    const sx = VW - 170;
    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(sx, 70, night() ? 22 : 28, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
    if (night()) { ctx.fillStyle = col('sky', dry); ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(sx - 10, 64, 20, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill(); }

    // far hills turning to dunes
    ctx.fillStyle = col('far', dry);
    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(0, 260);
    for (let x = 0; x <= W; x += 8) {
      const u = x + off * 0.12;
      const hill = 30 * Math.sin(u / 160) + 18 * Math.sin(u / 57 + 1.3);
      const dune = 34 * Math.pow(Math.abs(Math.sin(u / 120)), 0.6);
      ctx.lineTo(x, 215 - (hill * (1 - dry) + dune * dry));
    }
    ctx.lineTo(W, 260); ctx.closePath(); ctx.fill();

    // middle band of grass and trees
    ctx.fillStyle = col('mid', dry);
    ctx.fillRect(0, 255, W, 50);
    // lake
    if (lake > 0.02) {
      ctx.globalAlpha = lake;
      ctx.fillStyle = col('lake', dry);
      ctx.beginPath();
      const lx = 480 - ((off * 0.3) % 1400);
      for (const cx of [lx, lx + 1400]) ctx.ellipse(cx, 276, 260 * (0.5 + lake / 2), 9 + 5 * lake, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
    }

    const step = 90, o2 = off * 0.45;
    for (let i = Math.floor(o2 / step) - 1; i < (o2 + W) / step + 1; i++) {
      if (hash(i) > 0.15 + 0.75 * (1 - dry)) continue;
      const x = i * step - o2 + hash(i + 9) * 40, sc = 0.7 + hash(i + 3) * 0.6;
      tree(x, 268, sc * (1 - dry * 0.35), dry);
    }

    // ground and path
    ctx.fillStyle = col('ground', dry); ctx.fillRect(0, 290, W, H - 290);
    ctx.fillStyle = col('path', dry); ctx.fillRect(0, M.GROUND, W, 14);
    ctx.fillStyle = col('tuft', dry);
    for (let i = Math.floor(off / 37) - 1; i < (off + W) / 37 + 1; i++) {
      if (hash(i * 3.1) > 0.25 + 0.6 * (1 - dry)) continue;
      const x = i * 37 - off, y = 330 + hash(i) * 60;
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x, y); ctx.lineTo(x + 3, y - 9 * (1 - dry * 0.6)); ctx.lineTo(x + 6, y); ctx.fill();
    }

    for (const th of s.things) thing(th, K);
    group(K);

    // floating messages
    ctx.font = '600 13px Geologica Variable, sans-serif'; ctx.textAlign = 'center';
    ctx.lineWidth = 4; ctx.lineJoin = 'round'; ctx.strokeStyle = night() ? '#121a15' : '#ffffff';
    for (const f of s.fx) {
      ctx.globalAlpha = Math.max(0, 1 - f.age / 1.1);
      ctx.fillStyle = f.kind === 'water' ? K.water : f.kind === 'food' ? K.food : K.hurt;
      ctx.strokeText(f.text, f.x, f.y - 34); ctx.fillText(f.text, f.x, f.y - 34);
    }
    ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
  }

  function badge(cx: number, cy: number, colr: string) {
    ctx.font = '700 12px Geologica Variable, sans-serif'; ctx.textAlign = 'center';
    ctx.lineWidth = 3; ctx.strokeStyle = night() ? '#121a15' : '#ffffff';
    ctx.strokeText('×2', cx, cy); ctx.fillStyle = colr; ctx.fillText('×2', cx, cy);
  }

  function tree(x: number, y: number, sc: number, dry: number) {
    ctx.fillStyle = col('trunk', dry);
    ctx.fillRect(x - 2 * sc, y - 34 * sc, 4 * sc, 34 * sc);
    ctx.fillStyle = col('tree', dry);
    ctx.beginPath(); // flat-topped acacia
    ctx.ellipse(x, y - 38 * sc, 30 * sc, 9 * sc, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.ellipse(x - 12 * sc, y - 33 * sc, 16 * sc, 6 * sc, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();
  }

  function thing(th: M.Thing, K: typeof INK.day) {
    const { x, y, w, h } = th;
    ctx.save();
    switch (th.kind) {
      case 'water': {
        // a waterhole on the ground; a stone-lined well if you dug it
        const cx = x + w / 2, cy = y + h - 3;
        const wet = iconMode ? 1 : Math.min(1, M.localRain(s) / 0.7);
        const rw = (w / 2 + 6) * (0.65 + 0.35 * wet);
        ctx.fillStyle = K.mud;
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.ellipse(cx, cy, rw + 4, 7, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
        ctx.fillStyle = K.water;
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.ellipse(cx, cy, rw, 4.5, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
        ctx.strokeStyle = K.shine; ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(cx - rw * 0.4, cy - 1); ctx.lineTo(cx - rw * 0.1, cy - 1); ctx.stroke();
        if (th.bonus === 'wells') {
          ctx.fillStyle = K.rock;
          for (let i = 0; i < 9; i++) { const a = Math.PI * (i / 8); ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(cx - Math.cos(a) * (rw + 4), cy - Math.sin(a) * 3 + 2, 3.2, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill(); }
          ctx.strokeStyle = K.trunk; ctx.lineWidth = 2.5;
          ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(cx + rw + 2, cy); ctx.lineTo(cx + rw + 2, cy - 26); ctx.moveTo(cx + rw + 2, cy - 24); ctx.lineTo(cx - 4, cy - 30); ctx.stroke();
        } else if (wet > 0.6) {
          ctx.strokeStyle = K.stalk; ctx.lineWidth = 1.8;
          ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(cx + rw - 2, cy - 1); ctx.lineTo(cx + rw, cy - 15); ctx.moveTo(cx + rw + 2, cy); ctx.lineTo(cx + rw + 6, cy - 11); ctx.stroke();
        }
        break;
      }
      case 'fish': {
        if (M.has(s, 'harpoons') && !iconMode) badge(x + 15, y - 8, K.food);
        ctx.fillStyle = K.fish;
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.ellipse(x + 12, y + 9, 12, 6, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x + 22, y + 9); ctx.lineTo(x + 30, y + 2); ctx.lineTo(x + 30, y + 16); ctx.fill();
        break;
      }
      case 'grain': {
        if (M.has(s, 'wildgrain') && !iconMode) badge(x + 11, y - 8, K.food);
        ctx.strokeStyle = K.stalk; ctx.lineWidth = 2;
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x + 11, y + h); ctx.lineTo(x + 11, y + 8); ctx.stroke();
        ctx.fillStyle = K.grain;
        for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) { ctx.beginPath(); ctx.ellipse(x + 8 + (i % 2) * 6, y + 4 + i * 4, 3.5, 2.5, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill(); }
        break;
      }
      case 'game': {
        ctx.fillStyle = K.game; // a leaping gazelle
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.ellipse(x + 17, y + 13, 13, 6, -0.15, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.ellipse(x + 31, y + 6, 4, 3, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
        ctx.strokeStyle = K.game; ctx.lineWidth = 2;
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x + 28, y + 9); ctx.lineTo(x + 30, y + 6);
        ctx.moveTo(x + 32, y + 4); ctx.lineTo(x + 30, y - 4); ctx.moveTo(x + 33, y + 4); ctx.lineTo(x + 34, y - 4);
        ctx.moveTo(x + 8, y + 15); ctx.lineTo(x - 2, y + 24); ctx.moveTo(x + 26, y + 15); ctx.lineTo(x + 36, y + 24); ctx.stroke();
        break;
      }
      case 'field': {
        const fail = s.spellLeft > 0;
        for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
          const fx = x + 6 + i * 11;
          ctx.strokeStyle = K.stalk; ctx.lineWidth = 2;
          ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(fx, y + h); ctx.lineTo(fx + (fail ? 5 : 0), y + (fail ? 16 : 8)); ctx.stroke();
          if (!fail) { ctx.fillStyle = K.grain; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.ellipse(fx, y + 5, 4, 6, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill(); }
        }
        break;
      }
      case 'rock': {
        ctx.fillStyle = K.rock;
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x, y + h); ctx.lineTo(x + 4, y + 8); ctx.lineTo(x + 14, y); ctx.lineTo(x + 26, y + 6); ctx.lineTo(x + w, y + h); ctx.fill();
        break;
      }
      case 'thorn': {
        ctx.strokeStyle = K.thorn; ctx.lineWidth = 2.2; ctx.lineCap = 'round';
        ctx.beginPath();
        for (let i = 0; i < 7; i++) { const a = -Math.PI * (0.1 + 0.8 * (i / 6)); ctx.moveTo(x + w / 2, y + h); ctx.lineTo(x + w / 2 + Math.cos(a) * w * 0.55, y + h + Math.sin(a) * h); }
        ctx.stroke();
        break;
      }
      case 'dune': {
        ctx.fillStyle = K.dune;
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x, y + h); ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w * 0.35, y - 4, x + w * 0.62, y + 2); ctx.lineTo(x + w, y + h); ctx.fill();
        ctx.strokeStyle = K.duneEdge; ctx.lineWidth = 2;
        ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x + w * 0.62, y + 2); ctx.lineTo(x + w, y + h); ctx.stroke();
        break;
      }
    }
    ctx.restore();
  }

  function person(x: number, footY: number, phase: number, K: typeof INK.day, carry: 'pot' | 'spear' | null, airborne: boolean) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = K.ink; ctx.fillStyle = K.ink; ctx.lineWidth = 3.2; ctx.lineCap = 'round';
    const hip = footY - 22, neck = footY - 40;
    const sw = airborne ? 0.5 : Math.sin(phase) * 0.6;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x, hip); ctx.lineTo(x + Math.sin(sw) * 12, footY);
    ctx.moveTo(x, hip); ctx.lineTo(x - Math.sin(sw) * 12, footY);
    ctx.moveTo(x, hip); ctx.lineTo(x + 2, neck);
    ctx.moveTo(x + 1, neck + 4); ctx.lineTo(x + 1 - Math.sin(sw) * 9, hip + 2);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(x + 3, neck - 7, 6, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
    if (carry === 'pot') {
      ctx.fillStyle = K.pot;
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.ellipse(x + 3, neck - 19, 8, 6, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
      ctx.fillRect(x - 1, neck - 27, 8, 4);
    }
    if (carry === 'spear') {
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x + 1, neck + 4); ctx.lineTo(x + 6, hip + 2); ctx.moveTo(x - 6, hip + 8); ctx.lineTo(x + 18, neck - 16); ctx.stroke();
    }
  }

  function cow(x: number, footY: number, phase: number, K: typeof INK.day, size: number) {
    const b = Math.sin(phase) * 1.5;
    ctx.save(); ctx.translate(x, footY); ctx.scale(size, size);
    ctx.strokeStyle = K.cowSpot; ctx.lineWidth = 3; ctx.lineCap = 'round';
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(-12, -14); ctx.lineTo(-12 + Math.sin(phase) * 3, 0); ctx.moveTo(10, -14); ctx.lineTo(10 - Math.sin(phase) * 3, 0);
    ctx.stroke();
    ctx.fillStyle = K.cow;
    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.ellipse(0, -20 + b, 17, 9, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
    ctx.strokeStyle = K.cowSpot; ctx.lineWidth = 1.2; ctx.stroke();
    ctx.fillStyle = K.cowSpot;
    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.ellipse(-4, -22 + b, 6, 4, 0.3, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.ellipse(20, -24 + b, 6, 4.5, 0.4, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();
    ctx.lineWidth = 2; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(19, -28 + b); ctx.quadraticCurveTo(16, -38 + b, 10, -36 + b); ctx.moveTo(22, -28 + b); ctx.quadraticCurveTo(27, -38 + b, 32, -35 + b); ctx.stroke();
    ctx.restore();
  }

  function group(K: typeof INK.day) {
    const ph = reduce ? 0 : s.t * 12;
    if (M.has(s, 'cattle')) {
      const n = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(s.herd * 3));
      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) cow(M.PLAYER_X - 40 - i * 44, M.GROUND, ph + i * 1.7, K, 0.9 - i * 0.06);
    }
    if (s.hurt > 0 && !reduce && Math.floor(s.hurt * 12) % 2) return;
    person(M.PLAYER_X, s.y, ph, K, M.has(s, 'pottery') ? 'pot' : M.has(s, 'harpoons') ? 'spear' : null, !s.onGround);
  }

  // ---------- HUD ----------
  const fmt = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-GB');
  const ERA: Record<string, string> = { 'Green Sahara': 'the Green Sahara', 'The drying': 'the Sahara is drying', Desert: 'desert' };
  const MILESTONES: [number, string][] = [
    [5300, 'The rains are getting weaker'],
    [4500, 'The lakes are drying up'],
    [3500, 'The desert is spreading'],
    [2500, 'Only rivers, oases and the south stay green'],
  ];
  let msg = '', msgUntil = 0;
  function say(text: string, secs: number) { msg = text; msgUntil = s.t + secs; }

  function hud() {
    const b = Math.max(M.END_BCE, s.bce);
    $('h-ago').textContent = `${fmt(b + NOW - 1)} years ago`;
    $('h-year').textContent = `${Math.round(b)} BCE`;
    $('h-era').textContent = ERA[M.era(b)];
    for (const [k, v] of [['water', s.water], ['food', s.food]] as const) {
      $('b-' + k).style.width = `${Math.max(0, v)}%`;
      $('n-' + k).textContent = v < 20 ? 'low!' : `${Math.round(v)}`;
      $('b-' + k).parentElement!.parentElement!.classList.toggle('low', v < 20);
    }
    ways();
    for (const [y, text] of MILESTONES) if (s.bce <= y && s.bce > y - M.YEARS_PER_SEC * 0.1) say(text, 3.5);
    const ban = $('banner');
    const text = s.spellLeft > 0 ? 'Dry spell: the rains fail for years' : s.t < msgUntil ? msg : '';
    ban.hidden = !text; ban.textContent = text;
  }

  // ---------- councils ----------
  function situation(): string {
    const r = M.rainfall(s.bce);
    if (s.bce >= 6500) return 'The lakes are full and the grass is tall.';
    if (s.bce >= 5000) return 'The rains are becoming less reliable.';
    if (r > 0.3) return 'The lakes are drying up and the grass is thinning.';
    return 'The desert is spreading. Only rivers, oases and the south stay green.';
  }

  const WARN: Partial<Record<M.StrategyId, Record<string, string>>> = {
    harpoons: { weak: 'The lakes are shrinking: your fishing is failing', off: 'The lakes are gone: no more fishing' },
    wildgrain: { weak: 'Wild grain is thinning out', off: 'Too dry for wild grain now' },
    cattle: { weak: 'Not enough grass: your herd is shrinking' },
    sow: { weak: 'Dry spell: your fields are failing' },
  };
  const lastLevel: Record<string, string> = {};
  const lastTotal: Record<string, number> = {};

  const amount = (l?: M.Ledger) => {
    if (!l) return 'nothing yet';
    const items = [['food', l.food], ['water', l.water]] as const;
    const parts = items.filter(([, v]) => v >= 1).map(([k, v]) => `+${fmt(v)} ${k}`)
      .concat(items.filter(([, v]) => v <= -1).map(([k, v]) => `−${fmt(-v)} ${k}`));
    return parts.length ? parts.join(', ') : 'nothing yet';
  };
  const gaveText = (l?: M.Ledger) => {
    const items = l ? ([['food', l.food], ['water', l.water]] as const) : [];
    const gave = items.filter(([, v]) => v >= 1).map(([k, v]) => `${fmt(v)} ${k}`).join(' and ');
    const cost = items.filter(([, v]) => v <= -1).map(([k, v]) => `${fmt(-v)} ${k}`).join(' and ');
    if (gave && cost) return `It gave you ${gave} and cost you ${cost}`;
    if (gave) return `It gave you ${gave}`;
    if (cost) return `It cost you ${cost}`;
    return 'It made little difference';
  };

  function ways() {
    const ul = $('ways');
    if (ul.children.length !== s.chosen.length) {
      ul.innerHTML = s.chosen.map((id) => `<li data-id="${id}"><strong>${M.byId(id).name}</strong><span class="w-st"></span><span class="w-amt"></span></li>`).join('');
    }
    for (const li of Array.from(ul.children) as HTMLElement[]) {
      const id = li.dataset.id as M.StrategyId;
      const st = M.status(s, id), l = s.ledger[id];
      li.dataset.level = st.level;
      (li.children[1] as HTMLElement).textContent = st.text;
      (li.children[2] as HTMLElement).textContent = amount(l);
      const total = l ? l.food + l.water : 0;
      if (mode === 'run' && total - (lastTotal[id] ?? total) > 2) { li.classList.remove('pulse'); void li.offsetWidth; li.classList.add('pulse'); }
      if (mode === 'run' && Math.abs(total - (lastTotal[id] ?? total)) > 2 || lastTotal[id] === undefined) lastTotal[id] = total;
      const prev = lastLevel[id];
      if (prev && prev !== st.level && WARN[id]?.[st.level]) say(WARN[id]![st.level], 4);
      lastLevel[id] = st.level;
    }
  }

  function openGate() {
    mode = 'gate';
    const opts = M.council(s);
    if (!opts.length) { mode = 'run'; return; }
    $('g-sit').textContent = `${fmt(Math.round((s.bce + NOW) / 100) * 100)} years ago. ${situation()}`;
    const box = $('g-opts');
    box.innerHTML = '';
    opts.forEach((id, i) => {
      const st = M.byId(id);
      const b = document.createElement('button');
      b.type = 'button'; b.className = 'opt';
      const but = st.cost[0].toLowerCase() + st.cost.slice(1);
      b.innerHTML = `<span class="o-area">${st.area}</span><strong>${st.name}</strong><span class="o-gain">${st.gain}</span><span class="o-cost">But ${but}</span><span class="o-key" aria-hidden="true">${i + 1}</span>`;
      b.addEventListener('click', () => pick(id));
      box.appendChild(b);
    });
    $('ov-gate').hidden = false;
    (box.firstElementChild as HTMLElement)?.focus({ preventScroll: true });
  }

  function pick(id: M.StrategyId) {
    M.choose(s, id);
    $('ov-gate').hidden = true;
    hud();
    resume();
    if (s.chosen.length === 1) say(touch ? 'Tap to jump' : 'Space or tap to jump', 4);
  }

  // ---------- loop ----------
  function frame(ts: number) {
    if (mode !== 'run') return;
    const dt = Math.min(0.05, (ts - last) / 1000 || 0);
    last = ts;
    M.step(s, dt);
    scroll += M.SPEED * dt;
    if (M.gateDue(s)) { draw(); hud(); openGate(); return; }
    draw(); hud();
    if (s.over) { finish(); return; }
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  function resume() {
    mode = 'run';
    $('pause').hidden = false;
    last = performance.now();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  function start() {
    s = M.newState(); scroll = 0;
    $('ov-start').hidden = true; $('end').hidden = true;
    draw(); hud();
    $('stage').scrollIntoView({ behavior: reduce ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'center' });
    openGate(); // the first council, before setting out
  }

  function pause() {
    if (mode !== 'run') return;
    mode = 'pause'; $('ov-paused').hidden = false; ($('resume') as HTMLButtonElement).focus({ preventScroll: true });
  }

  // ---------- end ----------
  function path(): { title: string; who: string } {
    const h = (id: M.StrategyId) => M.has(s, id);
    if (h('move') && h('cattle')) return { title: 'You took the herds south', who: 'the herders who moved south into the Sahel, where cattle herding is still a way of life' };
    if (h('sow') && (h('move') || h('wells') || h('trade'))) return { title: 'You became farmers', who: 'the first sorghum and millet farmers on the southern edge of the Sahara' };
    if (h('move')) return { title: 'You followed the rain', who: 'the groups who left for the Nile valley and the south as the desert grew' };
    if (h('wells')) return { title: 'You dug in', who: 'the oasis communities who stayed by digging for water' };
    if (h('cattle')) return { title: 'You lived by your herd', who: 'the Saharan herders who moved their animals between pastures' };
    if (h('sow')) return { title: 'You became farmers', who: 'the first sorghum and millet farmers on the southern edge of the Sahara' };
    if (h('harpoons') || h('wildgrain')) return { title: 'You lived off the lakes', who: 'the lakeside foragers of the Green Sahara' };
    return { title: 'You found your own way', who: 'no single known group: a mix of ways of life' };
  }

  function finish() {
    mode = 'end';
    $('pause').hidden = true;
    const end = Math.max(M.END_BCE, s.bce);
    const ago = fmt(Math.round((end + NOW) / 10) * 10);
    const lasted = fmt(Math.round((M.START_BCE - end) / 10) * 10);
    const pth = path();
    const lock = (M.has(s, 'harpoons') || M.has(s, 'wildgrain')) && !M.has(s, 'cattle') && !M.has(s, 'move') && !M.has(s, 'wells') && !M.has(s, 'sow');
    const spells = s.events.filter((e) => e.text === 'Dry spell').length;
    const helped = s.events.filter((e) => e.text === 'Neighbours helped').length;
    const lines: string[] = [];
    if (s.over === 'won') {
      $('e-title').textContent = `${pth.title}, and made it`;
      lines.push(`Your people lasted all 7,000 years, to 1500 BCE (${ago} years ago).`);
      if (lock) lines.push('Living off lakes and wild grain rarely survived the drying. You were lucky, or very good at jumping.');
    } else {
      $('e-title').textContent = `${pth.title}, until the ${s.over} ran out`;
      lines.push(`Your people lasted ${lasted} years, until about ${ago} years ago (${fmt(Math.round(end / 10) * 10)} BCE). Then the group broke up and joined others.`);
      if (end > 5300) lines.push('The Sahara was still green. Dry spells and stumbles did it, not the big drying.');
      else if (lock) lines.push('Your way of life fitted the Green Sahara. When the lakes and wild grass went, there was nothing to fall back on.');
      else if (end > 3500) lines.push('The land dried faster than your way of life could change.');
      else lines.push('You held on deep into the desert age, after most groups had already left.');
    }
    lines.push(`Your choices look most like ${pth.who}.`);
    const moments = [];
    if (spells) moments.push(`went through ${spells} dry spell${spells > 1 ? 's' : ''}`);
    if (helped) moments.push(`were rescued by neighbours ${helped === 1 ? 'once' : helped === 2 ? 'twice' : `${helped} times`}`);
    if (M.has(s, 'cattle') && s.herd < 0.5) moments.push('watched your herd shrink');
    if (moments.length) lines.push(`Along the way you ${moments.join(', ').replace(/, ([^,]*)$/, ' and $1')}.`);
    $('e-text').innerHTML = lines.map((l) => `<p>${l}</p>`).join('');
    $('e-real').innerHTML = s.chosen.map((id) => {
      const l = s.ledger[id];
      const when = s.events.find((e) => e.text === M.byId(id).name)!.bce;
      const stopped = l && l.last > end + 500 && (l.food > 1 || l.water > 1) && id !== 'share'
        ? `, then stopped paying off around ${fmt(Math.round(l.last / 100) * 100)} BCE` : '';
      return `<li data-id="${id}"><strong>${M.byId(id).name}</strong>, chosen ${fmt(Math.round((when + NOW) / 100) * 100)} years ago. ${gaveText(l)}${stopped}.<span class="hind">Replaying history to check this choice…</span><span class="fact">${M.byId(id).real}</span></li>`;
    }).join('');
    chart();
    $('end').hidden = false;
    setTimeout(() => {
      const reviews = M.hindsight(s);
      const best = reviews.filter((r) => r.verdict === 'best').length;
      for (const r of reviews) {
        const el = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`#e-real li[data-id="${r.picked}"] .hind`);
        if (!el) continue;
        const others = M.STRATEGIES.filter((x) => s.councils.find((c) => c.picked === r.picked)!.options.includes(x.id) && x.id !== r.picked).map((x) => x.name);
        el.textContent = r.verdict === 'best' ? 'In hindsight: the best of the options you had.'
          : r.verdict === 'close' ? `In hindsight: about as good as ${others.join(' or ')}.`
          : r.years >= 100 ? `In hindsight: ${M.byId(r.best).name} would have kept your people going about ${fmt(r.years)} years longer.`
          : `In hindsight: ${M.byId(r.best).name} would have left your people better off.`;
        el.dataset.verdict = r.verdict;
      }
      const sum = document.createElement('p');
      sum.innerHTML = `<strong>In hindsight, ${best} of your ${reviews.length} choices ${best === 1 ? 'was' : 'were'} the best on offer.</strong> Below, see which ones weren’t, and what would have done better.`;
      $('e-text').appendChild(sum);
    }, 60);
    $('end').scrollIntoView({ behavior: reduce ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'start' });
  }

  function chart() {
    const svg = $('e-chart');
    const L = 40, R = 740, T = 14, B = 220;
    const X = (b: number) => L + ((M.START_BCE - b) / (M.START_BCE - M.END_BCE)) * (R - L);
    const Y = (v: number) => B - (v / 100) * (B - T);
    const line = (key: 'water' | 'food' | 'rain', cls: string) => {
      const pts = s.log.map((d) => `${X(d.bce).toFixed(1)},${Y(key === 'rain' ? d.rain * 100 : d[key]).toFixed(1)}`);
      return pts.length ? `<polyline class="${cls}" points="${pts.join(' ')}"/>` : '';
    };
    const ref = Array.from({ length: 141 }, (_, i) => { const b = M.START_BCE - i * 50; return `${X(b).toFixed(1)},${Y(M.rainfall(b) * 100).toFixed(1)}`; });
    let out = `<rect class="c-bg" x="${L}" y="${T}" width="${R - L}" height="${B - T}"/>`;
    // dry spells
    for (const e of s.events.filter((e) => e.text === 'Dry spell')) {
      const x0 = X(e.bce), x1 = Math.min(R, X(e.bce - 4.5 * M.YEARS_PER_SEC));
      out += `<rect class="c-spell" x="${x0}" y="${T}" width="${Math.max(2, x1 - x0)}" height="${B - T}"/>`;
    }
    out += `<polyline class="c-ref" points="${ref.join(' ')}"/>`;
    out += line('water', 'c-water') + line('food', 'c-food');
    for (let b = 8000; b >= 2000; b -= 1000) out += `<text class="c-ax" x="${X(b)}" y="${B + 18}" text-anchor="middle">${fmt(b)} BCE</text>`;
    out += `<text class="c-ax" x="${L - 6}" y="${Y(100) + 4}" text-anchor="end">100</text><text class="c-ax" x="${L - 6}" y="${Y(0) + 4}" text-anchor="end">0</text>`;
    const choices = s.events.filter((e) => e.text !== 'Dry spell' && e.text !== 'Neighbours helped');
    choices.forEach((e, i) => {
      const x = X(e.bce);
      out += `<line class="c-tick" x1="${x}" x2="${x}" y1="${B}" y2="${B + 6}"/><text class="c-choice" x="${x > R - 110 ? x : x + 3}" text-anchor="${x > R - 110 ? 'end' : 'start'}" y="${B + 36 + (i % 2) * 14}">${e.text}</text>`;
    });
    if (s.over !== 'won') out += `<line class="c-end" x1="${X(s.bce)}" x2="${X(s.bce)}" y1="${T}" y2="${B}"/>`;
    svg.innerHTML = out;
  }

  // ---------- input ----------
  const tryJump = () => { if (mode === 'run') M.jump(s); };
  cv.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => { e.preventDefault(); tryJump(); });
  window.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    if (mode === 'run' && (e.code === 'Space' || e.code === 'ArrowUp' || e.code === 'KeyW')) { e.preventDefault(); tryJump(); }
    else if (mode === 'run' && (e.code === 'KeyP' || e.code === 'Escape')) pause();
    else if (mode === 'pause' && (e.code === 'KeyP' || e.code === 'Escape')) { $('ov-paused').hidden = true; resume(); }
    else if (mode === 'gate' && /^Digit[1-3]$/.test(e.code)) {
      const b = $('g-opts').children[Number(e.code.slice(5)) - 1] as HTMLButtonElement | undefined;
      b?.click();
    }
  });
  $('go').addEventListener('click', start);
  $('again').addEventListener('click', () => { $('stage').scrollIntoView({ behavior: reduce ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'center' }); start(); });
  $('pause').addEventListener('click', pause);
  $('resume').addEventListener('click', () => { $('ov-paused').hidden = true; resume(); });
  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', () => { if (document.hidden) pause(); });
  document.addEventListener('themechange', () => draw());

  let iconMode = false;
  function icons() {
    const saved = ctx; iconMode = true;
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLCanvasElement>('canvas[data-icon]').forEach((c) => {
      const well = c.dataset.icon === 'well';
      const kind = (well ? 'water' : c.dataset.icon) as M.Kind;
      const dpr = Math.min(2, window.devicePixelRatio || 1);
      const bw = kind === 'field' ? 84 : 48, bh = 44;
      c.width = bw * dpr; c.height = bh * dpr; c.style.width = `${bw}px`; c.style.height = `${bh}px`;
      ctx = c.getContext('2d')!;
      ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0); ctx.clearRect(0, 0, bw, bh);
      const sz: Record<string, [number, number]> = { water: [34, 16], fish: [30, 18], grain: [22, 34], game: [34, 28], field: [70, 34], rock: [30, 24], thorn: [40, 30], dune: [64, 30] };
      const [w, h] = sz[kind];
      const k = kind === 'dune' ? 0.7 : 1;
      ctx.translate(bw / 2 - (w * k) / 2, 0); ctx.scale(k, k);
      thing({ kind, x: well ? -4 : 0, y: (bh / k) - h - 4, w, h, bonus: well ? 'wells' : undefined }, ink());
    });
    ctx = saved; iconMode = false;
  }

  fit(); draw(); hud(); icons();
  document.addEventListener('themechange', icons);
  (window as any).__dr = { get s() { return s; }, get mode() { return mode; } };
</script>

<style>
  .crumb { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .game { margin-top: 0.5rem; }

  .hud { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: end; gap: 0.75rem 2rem; margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
  .when { display: flex; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.3rem 0.9rem; }
  .when { flex-direction: column; align-items: start; gap: 0.15rem; }
  .ago { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.2vw, 2.1rem); line-height: 1.05; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .meters { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(10rem, 1fr)); gap: 0.4rem 1.4rem; flex: 1 1 22rem; max-width: 28rem; }
  .meter { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3.1rem 1fr 4.2rem; align-items: center; gap: 0.45rem; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .meter .lab { color: var(--muted); }
  .bar { height: 10px; background: var(--line); border-radius: 2px; overflow: hidden; }
  .bar i { display: block; height: 100%; width: 80%; transition: width 0.15s linear; }
  .m-water .bar i { background: #1f6fa3; }
  .m-food .bar i { background: var(--ochre-fill); }
  .m-rain .bar i { background: var(--moss); }
  :global([data-theme='night']) .m-water .bar i { background: #7cc0ea; }
  .num { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .meter.low .num { color: var(--ochre); font-weight: 600; }
  .t-water { color: #1f6fa3; } .t-food { color: var(--ochre); }
  :global([data-theme='night']) .t-water { color: #7cc0ea; }

  .stage { position: relative; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; touch-action: manipulation; user-select: none; -webkit-user-select: none; }
  #cv { display: block; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 960 / 400; cursor: pointer; }
  .stage { scroll-margin-top: 4rem; }
  .banner { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 0.8rem; transform: translateX(-50%); margin: 0; padding: 0.35rem 0.7rem; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ochre-soft) 92%, transparent); border: 1px solid var(--ochre); border-radius: 3px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pause { position: absolute; right: 0.6rem; top: 0.6rem; font: inherit; font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 85%, transparent); color: var(--ink); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; }

  .ov { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: grid; place-items: center; padding: 1rem; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg) 55%, transparent); overflow: auto; }
  .ov[hidden] { display: none; }
  .ov-box { max-width: 34rem; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem; }
  .ov-box.wide { max-width: 58rem; width: 100%; }
  .ov-box h2 { font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.6vw, 1.7rem); margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .ov-box p { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
  .keys { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .touch-only { display: none; }
  :global(.is-touch) .touch-only { display: inline; }
  :global(.is-touch) .no-touch { display: none; }
  .key-box { max-width: 44rem; }
  .key { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem; margin: 0.4rem 0 0.9rem; }
  .key h3 { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--muted); margin: 0.4rem 0 0.2rem; }
  .key ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .key li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; font-size: 0.92rem; padding: 0.1rem 0; }
  .key li.row3 { flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .key canvas { flex: none; }
  .key .row3 span { flex-basis: 100%; }
  .sit { color: var(--muted); }
  .opts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem; }
